WEBVTT

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.960
Argh, they were so close!

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.040
That makes it 5 games without loss.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.750
ETU's pretty good. Right?

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:41.550
We weren't defeated by Urawa, who we've lost to for three straight years.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.060
Maybe... we've really gotten better.

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:47.340
Yo.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.040
That was a great comeback game.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:54.380
You think so? You're making me blush.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.610
Hey, don't get cocky!

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:57.910
Hey, you two,

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.810
it's not like we won.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.830
What's there to fool around?

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.120
Understood!

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.830
Sorry!

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:11.560
The team is doing well, so you should be happy too.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.740
Well, let's go.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.480
Doing well, huh?

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.590
A counter!

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.060
Stop it!

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.860
That's dangerous!

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.720
Nice, Sugie!

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:39.950
Nice save!

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.600
We're being pushed too hard!

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.950
We're lacking concentration in both attack and defense!

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.310
We've been drawing for the past four games!

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:51.570
It'll be tough if we lose this one, Tatsumi!

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:56.710
And we're without Prince for today! Apparently, there's a problem with his foot.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.430
That guy's always quick to give in.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:06.270
I thought they were playing well until the match against Urawa,

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:09.230
but I never thought that it would get this bad.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:14.540
The draws against Shimizu and Urawa are good results since they were tough oppositions,

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:20.110
but we threw the lead away against Kofu and Yamagata.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:26.080
I'm not saying that a draw is bad, but...

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:32.200
if we keep playing like this, we'll probably lose today!

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.210
Akasaki!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.090
Too late, Hama!

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.550
Move it up, Hama!

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.220
What are you doing?!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.230
This is bad! Stop them immediately!

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.500
A foul?

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.130
A yellow card for Akasaki?

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.870
Why? Why was I booked?

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.790
Focus! They'll try to get a run in!

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:35.640
Right.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:39.450
Mark your man quickly!

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:43.680
Focus, focus! Don't let them push you over!

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:06.840
Why did I have to incur a yellow card?

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.020
What are you implying, Akasaki?

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:13.530
Are you saying that it's my fault that you were given a card?

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:14.480
Hama...

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:17.390
Don't you even know what you've done?

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:20.110
We were bombarded through the flanks!

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:24.910
You lose the ball, then let them past, and allow them to cross the ball...

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:27.740
All of you in fact, left and right.

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:30.740
Left... Wait, me too?!

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.990
I've been wondering for a while now.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:42.500
Aren't you guys disappointed that we've only drawn our matches?

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:46.420
It's good that you're having fun out there,

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:52.390
but does that attitude bode well with the team which desperately needs a win?

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:03.930
Unlike you, I really want to win!

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:07.650
If you guys want to take it easy, could you please do it somewhere else?

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.280
You bastard!

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:13.610
Alright. that's enough, Akasaki.

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.290
I truly understand how you feel.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:20.700
I do, but...

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.840
Damn, you're one stuck up brat!

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:26.440
What's with that attitude towards your seniors?!

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:29.330
What? This has nothing to do with you, asshole.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.120
Kuro!

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:31.400
Stop it!

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.600
Cut it out already!

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.680
Hey! Stop it!

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.700
You brat!

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:40.440
What's that, Akasaki?!

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:45.160
Does playing with that stern expression...

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:49.820
make you think you're being serious?!

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:54.820
Can someone who's not enjoying himself even play well?!

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:56.200
Hey, we're still having a match here!

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.150
Can you say that our teamwork is flawless?

00:07:58.150 --> 00:07:59.720
Wow, everyone's all psyched up!

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:02.070
I'm enjoying it in my own way!

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:05.800
They're scary.

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:06.710
Maybe you're enjoying yourself the wrong way.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:09.830
This is amazing!

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:11.620
Hey, Tatsumi...

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.850
Don't you think you should break them up?

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:18.970
I can't tolerate the fact that you guys are running around like little girls and messing up.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.720
What the hell did you say?

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.320
Akasaki, stop it.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.610
If you're a side-back, then do your job.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:29.120
I am! But it's not just offense I have to deal with!

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.790
We're losing! If we don't take risks...

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:36.620
If the midfield is packed, we can't push forward!

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.750
I don't see a problem with it. Just let them continue.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:43.000
What? W-Why would you?!

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:48.650
It's interesting.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:50.940
When it's a draw,

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:53.630
you can really see how the team is doing.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:01.060
For instance, when the players look disappointed after a match,

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.920
then this shows that there are still problems the team has to rectify.

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:10.580
On the other hand, if everyone looks contented,

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:13.400
it means that the team did their best for the tough match.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.000
Maybe you should quit playing soccer.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:15.900
What?!

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:20.040
I don't think this is the right time to say this...

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:24.050
Among the possible scenarios,

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:28.060
the worst is when everyone has a different look on their face,

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.670
like that of the team for the past few games.

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:36.400
That's what I've been saying!

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.900
Hama, stop it.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:40.700
You can't just run up like that!

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:47.350
Don't push up as and when you like; find the right time to do it.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.530
Understood.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:51.580
We didn't lose against Urawa this time.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.020
Yeah, we did well.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:56.570
We haven't won a game in a while!

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:02.290
We've gone on a winning streak after going through a losing one,

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:04.420
but now we've been drawing games.

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:08.580
It's hard to tell if we've gotten better or not.

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:13.710
ETU have been near the bottom for a very long time.

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:17.840
And also this year, we've got quite a few inexperienced youngsters.

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:23.120
Which is why the lack of cohesion isn't much of a surprise.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:26.890
But if it had come to this, I think we'll be all right!

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:36.170
Everyone develops differently.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.990
However, there's only one way to develop a team.

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:44.870
If you want to win,

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:50.250
then you'll have to find a compromise between each other, even if it is through quarreling.

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:53.660
Only then you'll understand what the others are thinking.

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:56.570
This will then propagate,

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:59.630
and the team will finally be able to work together work as a unit.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:10.520
That's how strong teams are created!

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:35.970
Phew, I thought we've imploded.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:39.340
Sera.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:43.800
I might throw you on during the second half. Warm up!

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.430
Yes! I'll be waiting!

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:26.100
I see. ETU lost yesterday...

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:32.690
Yes, 1-0 against Niigata. I thought you watched it.

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:35.610
Nope, I planned to...

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:42.110
But I thought about spotting our own weaknesses, so I watched our team's video instead.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:46.620
But then I got mesmerized...

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:52.620
by our strong, yet elegant football.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:03.510
What's with him? He's putting on such a confident expression!

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:10.260
That is why we are sitting comfortably undefeated on top of the league!

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:15.520
The manager of the Osaka Gunners does emit a different aura!

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:21.530
Stop it, Sonoda. There are people watching.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.160
But it's a real pity though.

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:27.990
What?

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:33.960
Though ETU haven't been at their best for the last few matches, they still managed to hold on.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:38.380
But they finally gave way.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:45.170
I'm Dulfer, a manager. My best wishes to you.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:48.580
Ah, hi.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:49.680
Nice to meet you.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:02.400
I'd hoped that he could get that team back on track,

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:07.740
Sonoda?

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:09.070
Yes?

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:17.040
He's going to be one hell of a manager.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:25.170
If we were to go against them, I would like to beat them when they're at their best.

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:30.220
Then, we'll be able to prove our strength.

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:35.220
Well, don't worry about that.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:41.060
Though ETU lost yesterday,

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:45.400
they played their opponents off the park during the 2nd half.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:46.900
Really?

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.410
Yes, it's like they've been revived.

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:53.740
They utterly dominated the whole of the half.

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:57.120
They increased their frequency of wing play, and No.20,

00:14:57.310 --> 00:15:03.880
who had just recovered from an injury, got a couple of nice direct passes.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:08.600
If the players had been in better shape,

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:11.460
and if the playmaker, Gino, had played,

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.390
the outcome could have been different.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.820
Is that so? Thank you, Sonoda.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:33.240
Seems like there's something to look forward to after today's match after all.

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.080
When we get back,

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:42.460
let's watch their game with a glass of wine.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:46.530
But before I can open that bottle of wine,

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:49.840
we'll have to beat our next opponent first!

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:11.820
Are you ready for battle, my proud, brave warriors?

00:16:29.850 --> 00:16:34.590
I think we played better in the second half.

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:47.410
There's still some pressing issues, but at least they've aligned themselves better.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:53.250
I can feel that everybody wants to win.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:57.240
Otherwise, they wouldn't have been disappointed about losing to Niigata.

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:03.680
Okay. Understood.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:07.970
Then I think we might be able to get a result against Osaka.

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:15.510
"Might be"? Are you confident?

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:21.770
Of course I am. Aren't you, Murakoshi?

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.400
What kind of player goes out on the field expecting to lose?

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:31.480
Isn't that right? Let's just sweep Osaka aside.

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:40.290
To do that, starting tomorrow, we'll be having an
intensive training programme for the Osaka match.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:41.790
Prepare yourself.

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:49.150
Does this guy already have a plan against Osaka?

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:54.700
How far has he been planning ahead?

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.830
Oh, I won! Lucky!

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:01.810
I think we might actually win against Osaka!

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:18.570
Why the glum face?

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:23.200
Tatsumi and Murakoshi! What time is it already? What are you guys doing?!

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:26.480
What do you mean?

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.580
I'm off to get my free popsicle.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:32.460
Things are turning bad!

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:39.970
Osaka's captain, Hirata, intercepts again!

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:48.940
He passes it to Shimura, the midfielder.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:56.270
Ahead of Shimura is... Hauer, Katayama, Hatake and Kubota.

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:58.950
The four forwards are gunning for the goal.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:02.900
This is Osaka Gunner's ultra attacking line-up they pride themselves in!

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:09.210
Here, here!

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.960
Hurry up and pass it here!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.980
Uh...

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:18.470
Got it!

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.090
Clear it, clear it!

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.990
Uh...

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:29.270
Kubo, here!

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.470
GOAL!

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:51.880
Hatake scores to get Osaka 4 up!

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:54.570
And it's only been 40 minutes!

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:58.170
Osaka's relentless assault has given Kofu a huge mountain to climb.

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:03.680
Top of the league with the most number of goals scored, Osaka Gunners.

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:10.450
Can anyone stop this ultra attacking set-up which manager Dulfer has come up with?

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:15.310
This is scary.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:18.480
This looks bad. Right, Tatsumi?

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.940
Huh? He's gone...

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:30.980
Vanguard Kofu
Osaka Gunners

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:34.960
See, I told you!

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:39.670
I knew that the Osaka-Kofu match was gonna be great!

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:42.920
It's not often you get to see a thrilling 8-0 game!

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:47.800
And you insisted on spectating another match.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:51.250
Geez, we have already informed the press,

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:53.980
but he only told me 30 minutes before the game started.

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:04.490
This thing's delicious. Where did you buy it?

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:08.580
Well, what do you want to do?

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:15.000
The next scheduled match is ETU-Osaka at the Sumidagawa stadium.

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:19.540
What are you talking about? Of course I'm going.

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:20.750
You don't get it, do you?

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:28.010
Osaka simply have to be observed since they're in top form now.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:35.770
Plus, I'm interested in how ETU will handle them.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:42.030
ETU? There's no one from there that's representing the nation, right?

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:51.970
I'm looking forward to it. What kind of football will you show me, Monsieur Tatsumi?

00:22:12.710 --> 00:22:17.630
Right, and that is all. Did everybody get it?

00:22:17.630 --> 00:22:19.310
Any questions?

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:22.070
What? That's all?

00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:36.830
Is this guy for real?

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:17.340
Can that really work?

00:24:17.340 --> 00:24:20.470
Osaka won by 8 goals yesterday.

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:23.280
Alright, I'm pumped up for this!

00:24:24.330 --> 00:24:25.850
Huh? Two forwards?!

00:24:26.520 --> 00:24:27.610
Tatsumi...
